1
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:20,900
Whether you're a fake using
his name or the real guy,

2
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,880
someday I'll kill you.

3
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:37,800
The first time Death Gun showed up was
after the second bullet of bullets.

4
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:42,940
And both of the murders he committed
happened in front of witnesses.

5
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,417
He's been staying under the
radar since the last killing,

6
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,794
probably leveling up as much as he can.

7
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:54,460
I don't see anyone
registered as Death Gun here,

8
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:57,133
but if he wants to stage another murder,

9
00:00:57,420 --> 00:00:59,680
B .O .B.'s perfect, he'll be here.

10
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:00,940
I know it.

11
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:05,480
I gotta find out the name of
Death Gun's Avatar and stop him.

12
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:37,077
I'm still so happy with my sweet love.

13
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:41,417
I'm still so happy with my love.

14
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:45,640
How can I get hurt?

15
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,397
I'm still so happy with my sweet love.

16
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:55,260
I'm still so happy with my pain.

17
00:02:05,120 --> 00:02:06,520
Oh?

18
00:02:57,460 --> 00:02:59,477
xenon hello anyone home?

19
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:02,217
come on shut up!

20
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,777
i thought i made it
clear i was done talking.

21
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:05,737
god, what else?

22
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:06,650
do you want from me?

23
00:03:06,733 --> 00:03:08,457
nothing but.

24
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:11,977
now that you mention it, maybe we could
swap some info before this starts.

25
00:03:12,060 --> 00:03:16,860
i mean, like you know, for old times sake?

26
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:22,100
Fine, whatever.

27
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:26,737
I'll do it, even though I'm the one
who's going to be giving all the info.

28
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:28,680
But I got stuff to share, too.

29
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:30,760
It's not a lot, but still.

30
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:42,980
How are you feeling?

31
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:44,637
You think you got a shot this time?

32
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:47,380
By the time he sees me, it'll be too late.

33
00:03:47,580 --> 00:03:48,900
This is crazy.

34
00:03:49,320 --> 00:03:51,600
Yeah, the final is like one big party.

35
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:54,330
Yeah?

36
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:56,137
For only a thousand creds,

37
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:59,397
I can hook you up with top-secret
info on all the top players!

38
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:01,720
Here goes, all on Yamikaze.

39
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,377
I wonder what hookahs odds are.

40
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:04,460
Come on, Dyne.

41
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:08,877
Sure he's got good gear and solid skills,
but that dude's older than hell, you know?

42
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:11,280
At best, he'd come in 15th today.

43
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:14,580
If you want to go with a
long shot, go with Richie.

44
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,920
So, you think I'm too old to get it on?

45
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:22,875
No, I was just saying, this
old dog's got some nitrous.

46
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,070
Hey, look!

47
00:04:24,153 --> 00:04:24,983
It's Kirito!

48
00:04:25,066 --> 00:04:27,345
She hacks up people good
with that Botox sword.

49
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:30,000
Ooh, a hot berserker with a blade.

50
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:32,597
Xenon's weren't my type, brother.

51
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,917
I wouldn't mind getting
a bullet for Xenon.

52
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:35,830
Roger that.

53
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:37,380
I'd rather get slashed.

54
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:39,700
And go play ALO with the fairies.

55
00:04:42,260 --> 00:04:43,220
Oh, sorry.

56
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:45,960
Yeah, you're Kirito. Sorry.

57
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:53,740
Hey, guys.

58
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,027
Hope you're all rude for me.

59
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:03,460
Yeah, you got it. Good luck out there.

60
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:05,266
I bet my life savings on you.

61
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:07,960
Oh, God.

62
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:09,633
Quit messing with them.

63
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:23,900
Okay, so 30 players get dropped
randomly across the same map,

64
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:28,897
and then you go around
shooting whoever you

65
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:31,568
find and the winner's
the last one standing?

66
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:33,760
Oh man, I knew it.

67
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:37,901
You're gonna make me explain the
whole damn thing to you after all.

68
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:39,975
Don't you have email?

69
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:43,597
The admin sent the rules out, so
it should be sitting in your inbox.

70
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:49,500
Yeah, I did scan through it, but it's
like I wanted to make sure I understood.

71
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,760
There was a lot of info to absorb.

72
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,310
Absorb.

73
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:57,917
Basically, you pretty
much got the gist of it.

74
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:01,765
This thing's a battle royale
between 30 players on the same map.

75
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,357
Star points are random,

76
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:06,497
and players are dropped about
1,000 meters away from each other.

77
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,000
Whoa, a thousand?

78
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:10,760
That's got to be one insanely huge map.

79
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:14,440
Honestly, you didn't
read the email, did you?

80
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:19,380
It's a multi-stage arena,
10 kilometers in diameter.

81
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:22,132
It's got mountains, forests, and deserts.

82
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:23,637
The start time's afternoon,

83
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:27,661
so there's no advantage or disadvantage
in terms of gear or skills.

84
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:30,960
How can you find anyone
in a field that big?

85
00:06:31,160 --> 00:06:32,177
That makes it challenging.

86
00:06:32,260 --> 00:06:34,440
It's a game with gunfights, remember?

87
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:38,197
Anyway, players get an item
to track other players.

88
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:40,337
It's called a satellite scan terminal.

89
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:41,596
There's a satellite?

90
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:44,300
Like a spy drone or something? Yep.

91
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,540
It works just like in real life.

92
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,980
It passes overhead every 15 minutes.

93
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:52,097
It scans the arena and then
transmits the coordinates

94
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:54,697
of all the players
directly to your terminal.

95
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:55,610
Neat, huh?

96
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:56,710
Hmm.

97
00:06:57,140 --> 00:07:01,580
So basically, you can only hide
in one spot for 15 minutes.

98
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:03,380
You catch on quick.

99
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:08,155
But then, doesn't all that moving
around put a sniper at a disadvantage?

100
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:11,857
Fifteen minutes is more than enough
time for a sniper to do their job.

101
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:14,540
I fire, I kill my target, I move on.

102
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:17,740
Oh, yeah, I guess.

103
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,440
So we good here? Great.

104
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,857
Next time we see each other,
you can bet your ass...

105
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:25,646
No, please, hold up, hold up!

106
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:30,932
Is there something else?

107
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,915
It's what I really want to talk about.

108
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:43,290
Hang on.

109
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:46,346
Could you take a look
at this list real quick?

110
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:47,817
Out of all the B .O .B.

111
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:51,577
contestants, are there any first-timers
whose names you don't recognize?

112
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:53,360
Okay, that's weird.

113
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:55,677
Please, just look at it and tell me.

114
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:56,642
It's important.

115
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:02,254
Well, if that's all you want
to know, I guess it's cool.

116
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:09,720
The first-timers I don't know, besides
a certain loser with a photon sword,

117
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:11,001
are three names.

118
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:13,220
That's great! Who? Point him out!

119
00:08:16,340 --> 00:08:20,097
Jushi X, Pale Rider, and...

120
00:08:20,180 --> 00:08:21,100
this guy.

121
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:22,930
Sterben?

122
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,440
Is one of them Death Gun?

123
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:32,801
You're going to tell me what this is about,
or are you going to keep me in the dark?

124
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:40,594
Getting ready to blow a fuse over here.

125
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,350
Speak up.

126
00:08:43,433 --> 00:08:46,417
I swear, if you're trying to make
me mess up today by pissing me off,

127
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,382
I'm going to...

128
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:50,097
No, that's not it.

129
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:52,020
It's just that...

130
00:08:53,540 --> 00:08:56,497
Does it have anything to do with
why you were acting weird yesterday?

131
00:08:56,580 --> 00:08:58,560
You know, after the prelims?

132
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,120
It does.

133
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:12,780
Yesterday, this person I once played
against in another VR MMO came up to me.

134
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:17,220
I'm pretty sure one of the
names you pointed out is him.

135
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,580
Is he a friend of yours?

136
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:22,220
No. An enemy.

137
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,020
I can't remember his name, though.

138
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:29,660
And I think we tried to kill each other.

139
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,160
Kill each other?

140
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:33,860
For real?

141
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:37,740
Was it like an argument
with someone in your party?

142
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,760
Something like that? No way.

143
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,180
It wasn't that.

144
00:09:41,400 --> 00:09:43,753
You don't kill someone over an argument.

145
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:46,620
Him and his group did horrible things.

146
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:49,140
Things like murder.

147
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:54,141
They were too far gone, and the
only way to stop them was by force.

148
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:56,720
I don't regret what I did,

149
00:09:57,120 --> 00:10:02,360
but still, I've avoided
taking responsibility for it.

150
00:10:02,980 --> 00:10:05,680
I forced myself to
forget it even happened.

151
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,260
For me,

152
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:15,520
there's no more running away, and this
time, I have to face what I did head-on.

153
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,380
Sorry to unload like that, just forget it.

154
00:10:21,220 --> 00:10:24,396
Do you think you could still
pull the trigger, though?

155
00:10:25,580 --> 00:10:28,817
Could you shoot a player
in here if you knew

156
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:31,724
in the real world that
player would die from it?

157
00:10:32,220 --> 00:10:34,573
And what if you had to kill that player?

158
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,353
Because if you didn't, you or
someone you love would die.

159
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:42,393
If you had that power, could
you still pull that trigger?

160
00:10:43,820 --> 00:10:47,114
Hirito, what's the name of
the game you met this guy in?

161
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:52,120
Sorry, never mind. That's personal.

162
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:54,240
No, that's okay.

163
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,270
Kirito

164
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:03,290
I

165
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:08,110
Sinon?

166
00:11:10,120 --> 00:11:12,677
We should start heading over
to the waiting dome now.

167
00:11:12,760 --> 00:11:14,477
We have to check our gear.

168
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:16,977
And get ourselves psyched
up for this battle.

169
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:18,257
Yeah, sure.

170
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:19,520
Lead the way.

171
00:11:35,660 --> 00:11:38,297
I get you've got your
reasons for being here.

172
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:39,500
Just like me.

173
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:41,950
But.

174
00:11:42,033 --> 00:11:44,640
It's got nothing to do
with that promise you made.

175
00:11:45,220 --> 00:11:46,537
I gotta pay you back.

176
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:48,914
For what happened in yesterday's final?

177
00:11:49,140 --> 00:11:49,970
Well, got it?

178
00:11:50,053 --> 00:11:52,800
You owe me a fight, so
you better stay alive.

179
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:54,800
Roger that.

180
00:11:55,060 --> 00:11:58,295
I promise I'll survive and
give you the fight you want.

181
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:01,370
Thanks.

182
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:11,497
If you're a battle junkie who loves
the smell of gun oil and gun smoke,

183
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:12,620
then get ready!

184
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:15,646
Place your bets, because
we're about to start!

185
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:17,190
Now,

186
00:12:17,340 --> 00:12:21,457
are you guys ready to find out who's
the strongest player in Gun Gale Online,

187
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:23,011
the hardest game in town?

188
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:33,820
As usual, MMO Stream will be broadcasting
the battle live and uncensored.

189
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:39,540
All right, help me out
with the countdown, guys.

190
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:48,700
10, 9, 8, 7, 6,

191
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:53,700
5, 4, 3, 2, 1!

192
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:57,600
The third bullet of bullets has begun!

193
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:18,110
Let's go.

194
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:44,460
Oh, my God.

195
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,390
Bingo.

196
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:21,780
Alright! Yeah! You go, girl!

197
00:14:35,280 --> 00:14:38,080
Twenty-one survivors left in play.

198
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:48,880
Looks like Dine's on the run.

199
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:52,497
Richie's got a heavy machine gun.

200
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:53,637
So he'll sit tight.

201
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:56,160
He likes his prey coming to him.

202
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:59,017
I'll go after Dine and Pale Rider.

203
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:03,940
I wonder how he's doing out there?

204
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:10,320
What the hell do I care?

205
00:15:33,380 --> 00:15:35,556
Damn, this guy's freaking persistent.

206
00:15:57,660 --> 00:15:58,490
Come on.

207
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:01,601
I got a mag full of rounds
with your name on them.

208
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:08,720
You forgot to check your six again, Dine.

209
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:09,800
See you later.

210
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:13,510
Who's there?

211
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:16,950
Shh.

212
00:16:18,380 --> 00:16:19,340
Keep it down.

213
00:16:19,620 --> 00:16:21,757
I need a favor. Are you kidding?

214
00:16:21,840 --> 00:16:23,840
It's too late for any more favors.

215
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:26,280
One of us dies right now.

216
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:27,730
Stop it.

217
00:16:27,813 --> 00:16:30,229
I don't want those guys
to know we're here.

218
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:31,520
What are you up to?

219
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:34,117
I want to watch what
happens on that bridge.

220
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,620
So don't shoot, okay?

221
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:37,910
Okay.

222
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:40,140
Then what? That depends.

223
00:16:40,320 --> 00:16:41,980
But I'm not here for you.

224
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:43,590
I'll leave after.

225
00:16:43,673 --> 00:16:44,503
Promise.

226
00:16:45,020 --> 00:16:47,717
The minute you turn your
back, I'll blow you away.

227
00:16:47,800 --> 00:16:49,377
If that's what you want, then fine.

228
00:16:49,460 --> 00:16:51,600
But for now, just stay quiet.

229
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:54,250
All right.

230
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:57,017
But after they're done down
there, it's you and me.

231
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:57,930
Okay.

232
00:17:08,940 --> 00:17:11,293
Your stealth skills are pretty pathetic.

233
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:19,097
I'm not letting him leave the area alive!

234
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:21,617
If he makes a move, I'm taking the shot.

235
00:17:21,700 --> 00:17:22,957
He's all yours.

236
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:24,500
Wait, company?

237
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:47,440
Oh, son of a...

238
00:17:50,020 --> 00:17:51,300
Damn it!

239
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:56,540
Damn it!

240
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:01,760
Whoa, he's fast.

241
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:06,420
He boosted his three-dimensional
mobility by carrying lighter gear.

242
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:12,520
His acrobatic skills are through the roof!

243
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:19,810
Bastard!

244
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:22,660
Gah!

245
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,030
Gah!

246
00:18:25,300 --> 00:18:26,130
Gah!

247
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:32,240
No!

248
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:52,760
If only he had time to switch mags,

249
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:55,637
he could have shot from the
hip and killed him easy.

250
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:56,550
That pale guy.

251
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:59,620
He's quick and powerful.

252
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:02,680
Maybe he's the one in the cloak.

253
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:03,960
An enemy.

254
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:07,524
I think we tried to kill
each other once before.

255
00:19:12,100 --> 00:19:13,460
I'm taking him out.

256
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:17,460
Okay, but it won't be
easy if he's who I think.

257
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,337
Oh, please.

258
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:21,900
He can't dodge my bullet at this range.

259
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:34,160
Did you hear a gunshot?

260
00:19:34,420 --> 00:19:35,420
There wasn't one.

261
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:38,060
What the hell's going on?

262
00:19:38,580 --> 00:19:39,760
Two possibilities.

263
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:43,177
It could have been a laser
rifle with a muffled blast.

264
00:19:43,260 --> 00:19:45,760
Or maybe a live ammo gun with a silencer.

265
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:48,980
Either way, it wasn't a kill shot.

266
00:19:49,300 --> 00:19:50,920
So why isn't he moving?

267
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,635
I think the shot came from the forest.

268
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:55,070
Uh-uh.

269
00:19:55,153 --> 00:19:57,317
He was sniped from further away than that.

270
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:59,812
I did a scan of the map not too long ago.

271
00:19:59,940 --> 00:20:02,528
There's no one within
one kilometer of here.

272
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:07,137
And now that we're on the subject, you
mind telling me where you came from?

273
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:10,220
Uh, I was chasing after
that pale rider guy.

274
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,790
Hang on.

275
00:20:11,900 --> 00:20:13,840
Oh, no way. What's up?

276
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:17,977
When the satellite was scanning the
area, I was swimming in that river.

277
00:20:18,060 --> 00:20:22,057
I guess my location didn't register
on the map because I was underwater.

278
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:23,017
Was all that gear?

279
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:23,930
You should have drowned.

280
00:20:24,013 --> 00:20:26,240
Nah, I took it all off before I dove in.

281
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:28,067
Stuck it in my item storage.

282
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:33,757
I never knew we could use the
river for cover from the satellite.

283
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:34,958
Thanks for the tip.

284
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:36,580
I'll keep it in mind.

285
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:40,100
Xenon, check out his shoulder.

286
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:42,087
There's a weird light there.

287
00:20:44,980 --> 00:20:46,240
A stun bullet!

288
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,580
How long's he been there?

289
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:14,960
He's got a silent assassin.

290
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:17,222
Is that what his rifle's called?

291
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:18,630
Yeah.

292
00:21:18,713 --> 00:21:22,105
It's a high-end sniper rifle
that's got a badass silencer on it.

293
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:27,640
I heard rumors about there being one
in GGO, but I've never seen it before.

294
00:21:28,720 --> 00:21:32,780
If he can handle that gun,
he must be some player.

295
00:21:49,060 --> 00:21:51,825
Why would he use his
handgun to finish him off?

296
00:21:54,520 --> 00:21:57,520
Xenon, shoot! Huh? Which one?

297
00:21:57,760 --> 00:21:59,097
It's the guy in the cloak!

298
00:21:59,180 --> 00:22:00,117
There's no time!

299
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:01,030
Shoot him!

300
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:02,370
Hurry!

301
00:22:02,453 --> 00:22:03,660
Don't let him fire that gun!

302
00:22:45,440 --> 00:22:51,237
Sugou kieru nukumori Nori
hi to tsunomai yoranai

303
00:22:51,320 --> 00:22:57,757
yo Mito kuyoku to tsuyoku

304
00:22:57,840 --> 00:23:02,557
Knight to mega ta Kukamimi

305
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:05,997
mo kakagellu Kodok na

306
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:10,440
koshino Yuna koko no Back ku

307
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:38,040
Next time, Death Gun.

308
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:41,740
Thank you.
